# Neo Learn Physical parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.6). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnPhysical
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnPhys
class NeoLearnPhysicalMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching physical-modelling synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A bank of 32 resonating modes (a string, tube, bar or plate, and everything between) with a material from wood through nylon and glass to metal, struck, plucked or bowed, and anything between, with force, damping and body size, an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for marimbas, plucked strings, glass bowls, bells and bowed or breathy tones, or to learn how modal synthesis works.

group Core
Material         "Material" 0 1000 200 pct
    id material
    how Shifts modal frequency ratios and high-frequency internal damping along a continuum (Wood -> Nylon -> Glass -> Metal).
    sound Morphs the resonant body from warm marimba wood to nylon string, glassy crystal, and ringing bronze.
ExciterType      "Exciter Mode" 0 1000 0 pct
    id exciter_type
    how Morphs the physical energy source from a momentary strike (0% Mallet), to a sharp pluck (50% Pick), to sustained friction/air (100% Bow/Breath).
    sound Switches the instrument behavior between struck percussion, plucked strings, and sustained wind/bowed tones.
ExciterForce     "Strike / Pressure" 0 1000 500 pct
    id exciter_force
    how Controls the hardness of the mallet/pick impulse or the turbulence/velocity of the bow/breath stream.
    sound Low values sound soft, felt-like, or breathy; high values produce sharp, bright, forceful attacks.
ResonatorShape   "Geometry" 0 1000 0 pct
    id resonator_shape
    how Reconfigures the harmonic spacing of the modal filter bank (String -> Open Tube -> Bar -> Hollow Plate).
    sound Alters the acoustic geometry from a 1D string or flute pipe to a 2D metallic plate or drum shell.
Damping          "Damping" 0 1000 300 pct
    id damping
    how Controls the rate of energy absorption inside the resonator, especially for upper frequency modes.
    sound High damping mutes the ring quickly like palm-muted strings; low damping lets notes ring out freely.
BodySize         "Body Size" 0 1000 500 pct
    id body_size
    how Shifts the acoustic formant cavity filter attached to the output of the resonator.
    sound Scales the perceived acoustic body from a tiny thumb piano or piccolo up to a cello or concert hall marimba.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 150 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 812 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 1000 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 577 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 644 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnPhysicalMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
